@startuml dispense-flow
title One dispense: from main down to the stock check

skinparam dpi 150
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FEFECE

start
:**PharmacyTracker (main)**
pharmacy.dispense(customer, medication, qty, prescriber);

:**Pharmacy**
validate input: customer and medication not null, qty > 0;
if (input valid?) then (no)
  :throw IllegalArgumentException
(a programming error, not a business refusal);
  stop
endif

:**Category**
checkCanDispense(name, prescriber);
if (prescriber required
AND missing or blank?) then (yes)
  :throw MissingPrescriberException
"Cannot dispense <name> without a prescriber";
  :**main** catches and prints the message;
  note right: Nothing changed (same as the original)
  stop
endif

:**Pharmacy**
total = price x qty
total = customer.getKind().applyDiscount(total);

:**Medication**
removeStock(qty);
if (qty > stock?) then (yes)
  :throw InsufficientStockException
"Cannot dispense <qty> x <name>: only <stock> in stock";
  :**main** catches and prints the message;
  note right
    NEW behaviour (the one allowed change):
    refuse instead of going negative.
    Nothing is recorded.
  end note
  stop
endif
:**Medication**
stock = stock - qty;

:**Pharmacy**
customer.recordInHistory("Got <qty> x <name>")
create DispenseRecord and add it to transactions
return the record;

:**PharmacyTracker (main)**
reportPrinter.printDispense(record)
"Dispensed <qty> x <name> to <customer> [(prescribed by X)] for GHS <total>";
stop
@enduml